    "narrative": "For the Austin Waves on this August 17th slate, **Kyle Tucker** (85.90) headlines our offensive attack. His matchup against Tomoyuki Sugano is the gold standard for today\u2019s projections, bolstered by an elite 19% SP skill advantage and a park factor (+14%) that perfectly aligns with his power profile. **Andy Pages** (74.42) and **Drake Baldwin** (71.20) round out our tier-one plays. **Andy Pages** benefits from that same favorable park environment against Sugano, while **Drake Baldwin** leverages a significant 19% SP skill edge against Bailey Ober to vault into elite territory despite a modest base projection.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved balancing the volume of marginal starters against our limited game caps. **Jacob Wilson** (59.20) narrowly made the cut as our most efficient middle-tier option, holding off a cluster of players in the 47\u201353 range. **Gunnar Henderson** (52.61) and **Jackson Merrill** (53.97) were essentially toss-ups, but both are started despite concerns; **Gunnar Henderson** faces a significant 15% platoon drag against Shane McClanahan, while **Jackson Merrill** is hampered by a negative park factor and a difficult matchup against Nolan McLean. **Coby Mayo** (47.65) was the final inclusion, though his value is suppressed by his spot in the batting order and his disadvantage against McClanahan. \n\nLooking at the bench, our decision to leave the remaining depth out of the lineup is largely a function of availability and efficiency. With **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** sidelined on the IL, and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Heliot Ramos** facing team off-days, we are leaning heavily on the active roster to avoid burning caps on low-upside outings. We remain mindful of the \"Lineup Pending\" status for all starters; if official lineups shift **Liam Hicks**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Dominic Smith**, or **Luis Robert Jr.** significantly down the order, their efficiency scores will crater, necessitating late-minute pivots to reserves like **Nasim Nunez**, **Josh Jung**, **Curtis Mead**, **Wade Meckler**, or **Luis Lara** to preserve our season-long pacing.",
